    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d687">

                <pb facs="0849" n="739" sameAs="frus:frus1931v03/pg739"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.003/544: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-03-03T15:00:00+08:00">March 3, 1931—3
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received March 4—6:03 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>The Japanese Chargé, Shigemitsu, has just told me that on February 28 Ambassador
                        Debuchi<anchor n="41" xml:id="d687-f1"/> was informed by Assistant Secretary
                    Castle of the Department’s decision to drop negotiations on extraterritoriality
                    with Dr. C. C. Wu at Washington, owing to dissatisfaction with the Chinese
                    Minister’s attitude, wherefore negotiations had been transferred to China.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d687-f1" n="41" xml:id="d687-f1-content">
                <p>Katsuji Debuchi, Japanese Ambassador in the United States.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
